# AU DIC Benchmark Evaluation Framework — Implementation Plan (Sprint 002)

## Overview
With **Sprint 001** and the **Dedicated Normalization Layer** fully implemented and verified (100% test pass rate), we now move into **Sprint 002: Field-Level Extraction Evaluators & Semantic Category Matching**.

Sprint 002 builds deep evaluation logic on top of canonical representations to measure field-specific extraction accuracy (Candidate Name, Roll Number, Issue Date, CGPA, Subject Grades) and generate confusion matrices across document types.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Semantic Evaluation Policy**:
> - Comparators operate on **Canonical Representations** produced by `CanonicalNormalizer`.
> - Evaluates semantic correctness (e.g. `VTU` matching `Vivekananda Technical University`, `2021-IT-000150` matching `2021IT000150`, `14/07/2025` matching `2025-07-14`).
> - Produces detailed field-level error breakdowns in `comparisons.json`.

